<title>USA: Motorola to test cellular network in China.</title>
<headline>Motorola to test cellular network in China.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Thursday its Asia Pacific Cellular Infrastructure Group plans to install a trial CDMA (Code Division Multiple Access) cellular network in mainland China.</p>
<p>Through an agreement with Beijing Telecommunications Administration and Telecommunications Development Department of the China Electronic System Engineering Co, Motorola will install the network for 43,000 subscribers throughout Beijing.</p>
<p>The Bejing test is the first of a limited number of large-scale commercial trials planned by the national-level Beijing Telecom Great Wall joint planning office.</p>
<p>	  ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
